cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or refer to this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Tephra: an eBPF runtime threat-detection sensor for Kubernetes"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "MD Naved Raja"
    family-names: "Khan"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-0426-2822"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tephrasec/tephra"
url: "https://navedkhan.dev/"
abstract: >-
  An eBPF sensor that watches process, file and network activity on
  Kubernetes nodes from the Linux kernel, attributes each event to its pod,
  container and image, detects post-exploitation techniques with YAML rules,
  and can block a small set of high-confidence actions through LSM hooks.
  Coverage is measured with an attack harness and held-out evasion scenarios,
  and node overhead with published benchmarks.
keywords:
  - ebpf
  - kubernetes
  - runtime security
  - intrusion detection
  - linux kernel
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - GPL-2.0-only
